@title Matchmaking and Game Servers
@subtitle Embergate Online live architecture
@author Backend Services
@date 2026-09-22
@width wide

# Overview
Players are matched into 10-player games and placed on the nearest regional game server fleet. Each region can run alone if another region fails.

!! The Player Profile Database and the Leaderboard Service are the only shared parts. Watch them first in any regional failover.

# Architecture
diagram arch dir=LR title="Matchmaking and game servers"
arch: players "Players" user
arch: edge "Global Edge" lb "routes to closest region"
arch: mm "Matchmaker" svc
arch: alloc "Session Allocator" svc
arch: fleet "Game Server Fleet" svc
arch: cache "Regional Cache" cache
arch: profile "Player Profile Database" db focus
arch: lb "Leaderboard Service" svc focus
arch: players -> edge : connect
arch: edge -> mm : queue request
arch: mm -> cache : skill ratings
arch: mm -> profile : load profile
arch: mm -> alloc : match of 10
arch: alloc -> fleet : start session
arch: players -> fleet : UDP game traffic
arch: fleet -> lb : match results
arch: group region "Regional Stack (same in each of 3 regions)" mm, alloc, fleet, cache
arch: group shared "Shared across regions" profile, lb
arch: legend

# Regions and capacity
kpi Servers per region | 150 | scales to 400
kpi Players per region | 9,000 | concurrent
kpi Median match time | 10 s | target
kpi p95 match time | 30 s | target

table = region,game servers,matches per server,concurrent players; us-east,150,6,"9,000"; eu-central,150,6,"9,000"; ap-southeast,150,6,"9,000"

Each server runs 6 matches of 10 players. A region scales up to 400 game servers when more than 2,000 players are waiting in its queue.
